 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 42,
   "y": 33,
   "text": "COIRE GABHAIL, the LOST VALLEY. A secret hollow between two of the Sisters. The MacDonalds are said to have hidden stolen cattle here, since you couldn't see it from the glen below. A hidden valley, a great hiding place and a very steep walk. You're in good company."
  },
  {
   "x": 42,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "A HIDDEN COIRE. The hill folk call a hollow like this a coire, 'a cauldron'. This one fills with mist at the drop of a hat, so tread softly. If you hear an eagle, say hello. If an eagle says hello, say it back."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 60,
   "text": "GLENCOE MEMORIAL. In February 1692, soldiers who had been guests of the MacDonalds turned on them in the snow, and about thirty people died, many more fleeing into the hills. It's remembered here quietly. Walk gently, and stay a while."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 44,
   "text": "GLEANN COMHANN, GLENCOE. A glen made by ice, with sides so steep that the mist sits in the bowl like milk in a cup. Bidean nam Bian, at 1,150 m, is the highest hill in Argyll. The glen is a place to look up at."
  },
  {
   "x": 28,
   "y": 30,
   "text": "THE THREE SISTERS. Beinn Fhada, Gearr Aonach and Aonach Dubh: three great spurs of rock standing shoulder to shoulder. Walkers love them. Film crews love them. Bond came here, and so did a boy wizard, and neither of them could get a signal."
  }
 ],
